# Direct dependencies -- the ONLY hand-edited dependency file in this tree.
#
# Do not add pins here for libraries the application does not import directly:
# that is what requirements.lock is for. Edit this file, then regenerate:
#
#     pip-compile --output-file=requirements.lock requirements.in
#
# requirements.txt is a POINTER to that lock (it contains `-r requirements.lock`
# and nothing else), so `pip install -r requirements.txt` and
# `pip install -r requirements.lock` install byte-identical sets, and there is
# exactly one file whose contents a machine wrote. requirements.lock is
# committed on purpose: an unpinned transitive is a dependency nobody chose,
# resolved at install time, and it is the reason a green suite can go red on a
# commit that changed no Python.
#
# The `==` pins below are deliberate and load-bearing, so they stay in the .in
# rather than floating: each one is a version-sensitive decision, and the reason
# is written next to it. Dropping a pin here and letting the compiler choose
# would make those decisions silently.
Django==6.1.1
djangorestframework==3.18.1
djangorestframework-simplejwt==5.5.1
django-cors-headers==4.9.0
# SPEC-20-9: scannable MFA enrollment QR from the otpauth:// provisioning
# URI (common/qr.py). Pure Python, no runtime dependencies, emits SVG
# without an image library.
segno==1.6.1
razorpay==2.0.1
# SPEC-22-01: production Postgres. Django's postgresql backend loads psycopg3
# at first connection, so without this the documented postgres DATABASE_URL
# crashes the moment prod takes its first query. [binary] ships prebuilt
# libpq wheels (no compiler needed in the image).
psycopg[binary]==3.3.6
# SPEC-22-04 [R-22.13]: error tracking, imported ONLY when SENTRY_DSN is set
# (config/settings.py _init_error_tracking). Without a DSN the package is
# never imported, so the app boots and behaves exactly as it did before it
# was added - which is also why the test suite never needs it: the SDK init
# is stubbed. Official SDK, pinned like everything else here.
sentry-sdk==2.71.0
# WSGI server for config.wsgi (the Dockerfile CMD); Django's dev server is
# not a production server.
gunicorn==26.2.0
# Serves STATIC_ROOT from the app process, so DEBUG=false deployments still
# ship admin CSS/JS without a separate web server or object store.
whitenoise==6.11.0
python-dotenv==1.2.3
Pillow==12.3.0
coverage==7.16.1
# GATE-1 (2026-10-04): ruff is both the linter and the FORMATTER OF RECORD
# for this tree (config: backend/pyproject.toml; gate: the `lint` job in
# .github/workflows/backend-tests.yml). Pinned like everything else above
# because formatter output is version-sensitive -- the pin is what makes a
# local run and a CI run agree byte for byte, and dropping it would let the
# gate silently start reformatting on whatever ruff is current.
ruff==0.16.10
# MUT-1: mutmut, the automated mutation runner behind
# .github/workflows/mutation-weekly.yml. Weekly and workflow_dispatch only --
# it never runs on a pull_request, so it cannot gate one.
#
# 2.5.1 and NOT the current 3.8.0, and the reason is not age. mutmut 3 takes
# `pytest>=6.2.5` as a HARD requirement (its own metadata), and this repo's
# floor is measured by `manage.py test`; adopting 3.x would mean carrying a
# second test runner whose result is not the number the changelog prints.
# 2.5.1 takes any command as its runner, so the project's own runner is used
# unchanged. Its base install is also pytest-free (pytest is only an extra).
#
# Config is [tool.mutmut] in backend/pyproject.toml. Two gotchas measured while
# wiring this up, both of which cost a run before they were understood:
#   - `runner` IS read from that config file. mutmut declares `--runner` with
#     no default, so the value click passes is None (falsy) and the config
#     merge substitutes the file's value; the non-empty pytest runner is only
#     that merge's Python fallback. `--runner` on the command line is therefore
#     an OVERRIDE of the file's value, not a requirement. paths_to_mutate and
#     the boolean flags below are read from the file for the same reason: their
#     defaults are falsy too.
#   - `simple_output` does not disable the progress spinner; `no_progress`
#     does. With only simple_output set, mutmut dies on a cp1252 console with
#     UnicodeEncodeError on the braille character it writes to stdout.
mutmut==2.5.1